  "worked_solution": "We substitute each value into the given inequality and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $v=1$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7v & \\le 28 \\\\ 7\\cdot 1 & \\le 28 \\\\ 7 & \\le 28\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $v=1$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $v=1$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $v=3$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7v & \\le 28 \\\\ 7\\cdot 3 & \\le 28 \\\\ 21 & \\le 28\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $v=3$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $v=3$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $v=4$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7v & \\le 28 \\\\ 7\\cdot 4 & \\le 28 \\\\ 28 & \\le 28\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $v=4$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $v=4$ **satisfies** this inequality.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
